<title>UK: Dresdner to realign fund management - paper.</title>
<headline>Dresdner to realign fund management - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's Dresdner Bank is expected on Friday to unveil a restructuring of its international fund management operations, the Guardian newspaper reported.</p>
<p>The bank will place its London-based fund management arm -- Kleinwort Benson Investment Management -- under the control of RCM Capital Management, the San Francisco-based investment group acquired by Dresdner in June for $300 million, the paper said.</p>
<p>The move would create a global business based in the United States with managed funds of $30 billion.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
